            "review_title": "Review at Thai Express",
            "review_text": "JSTrip_77\nSarajevo, Bosnia and Herzegovina1194 contributions\n0\nGood Food, Service A Bit Slow\nMar 2019 • Couples\nTo start out, I hadn't noticed that a large party covering multiple tables had sat down, perhaps, right after we did. So, that could certainly account for the slower service we experienced. Otherwise, this was a very good meal. Although I'd say that this is the most expensive Thai restaurant I've been to in metro-Hanoi, it wasn't outrageous. That said, meals were approaching western prices, something that is normally quite easy to avoid in Hanoi. That said, my tom kha gai (chicken coconut soup) was delicious as was my Thai beef salad. The papaya salad was great too. But with all of the dishes, be careful not to eat one of the tiny little red pepper slices!! The pad Thai, was pretty exceptional. \n\nBut, like I mentioned, the service was a bit slow. We had to ask for our check twice and the glasses for the soft drinks had four or five tiny little melting ice chips. I cannot fault them for that. Some cultures don't really like ice. We just asked for more and they brought plenty. No problem. Would I go back? Well, it was expensive and the service wasn't great. There are TONS of restaurants in this area so I'd probably stick to the other Thai options.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 10, 2019",
